{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"hub","type":"text","text":"# The Mihogoni / Lake Cycle\nA linked story world, not a single story. Kalemie is story #1 — each story stands alone for competitions, but shares world, motifs, and cast with the others.\n\nSee [[Collection Tracker]].","x":-180,"y":-380,"width":460,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"motif-lake","type":"text","text":"**Motif: The Lake**\nEntropy · Memory · Women · Death · Colonial history.\nMust start neutral on the page and *accrue* meaning — never announce itself. See [[Composition]] (Symbolic Ascension).","x":-900,"y":-560,"width":300,"height":170,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"motif-debris","type":"text","text":"**Motif: Debris / Dead Things**\nDaudi's wall of collected junk — a private theology of refusing to let anything be forgotten.","x":-900,"y":-350,"width":300,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"motif-transport","type":"text","text":"**Motif: BMW vs. Dala Dala**\nClass made physical. Mode of transport as a form of antagonism, not just detail.","x":-900,"y":-160,"width":300,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story1","type":"text","text":"**Story #1 — Kalemie**\nPOV: Daudi\nStatus: Drafting\nTarget: Commonwealth Short Story Prize\nControlling Idea: *Inaction is complicity because choosing not to act is still a choice.*","x":-420,"y":40,"width":300,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"story2","type":"text","text":"**Story #2 — idea / trunk**\nCandidate POV: D'juma or Djamela\nStatus: Idea\n\nShould argue a *different* position in the Idea/Counter-Idea family than Kalemie, not repeat it in a new setting.","x":-60,"y":40,"width":300,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"story3","type":"text","text":"**Story #3 — idea / trunk**\nCandidate POV: Morisho, or a character not yet written\nStatus: Idea\n\nPull from [[Craft Log]]'s Cut / Original Material Archive for reusable fragments.","x":300,"y":40,"width":300,"height":190,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"char-daudi","type":"file","file":"01 Projects/Kalemie/02 Characters/Protagonist - Daudi.md","x":-1280,"y":60,"width":280,"height":100},
